# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO MCTB CANONICAL PRODUCT MAP

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-CANONICAL-PRODUCT-MAP.md`  
**Prerequisite:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PRODUCT-SCOPE-AND-DOMAIN-RULES.md` + `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-INFORMATION-ARCHITECTURE-AND-NAVIGATION-MAP.md` + `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-INVENTORY-AND-ROUTE-MANIFEST.md` (`.cursor/rules/transovo-mctb-product-scope.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/transovo-mctb-ia-navigation.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/transovo-mctb-page-manifest.mdc`)  
**Applies with:** All 15 `.cursor/rules/transovo-*.mdc` standards (always).

## When this rule activates

**Before any work** touching Missed Call Text Back — UI, API, `src/lib/mctb/`, `src/lib/agents/missed-call-text-back/`, voice/MCTB routes, consent, SMS recovery, onboarding, setup, analytics, exclusions, or related Prisma models — you **MUST read product scope first**, then the IA/navigation map, then the page manifest, then the full canonical map.

Paths include (not exhaustive): `src/components/mctb/**`, `src/app/**/voice/**`, `src/app/api/mctb/**`, `src/app/api/telnyx/voice/mctb*`, `src/lib/mctb/**`, `src/lib/agents/missed-call-text-back/**`, `src/app/f/mctb/**`, `src/app/(app)/onboarding/mctb/**`.

## Hard requirements

1. **Read `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PRODUCT-SCOPE-AND-DOMAIN-RULES.md` FIRST** — then `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-INFORMATION-ARCHITECTURE-AND-NAVIGATION-MAP.md` — then `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-INVENTORY-AND-ROUTE-MANIFEST.md` — then `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-CANONICAL-PRODUCT-MAP.md` — then apply all Transovo standards guides.
2. **Screenshots and current UI are evidence only** — not authority for IA, nav, or page placement.
3. **Preserve runtime** — Audit → Preserve → Extend → Consolidate. Do not rewrite working telephony/SMS/consent pipelines without explicit approval.
4. **One canonical home** per feature — no duplicate sidebar destinations for setup subsections.
5. **Mental model:** configure → missed call → eligibility/consent → text-back → reply → follow-up → measure.
6. **Consent (Guide #8):** No `consent = true` model. `press_1` and `existing_consent` are different provenance paths.
7. **Three state families:** SENDER / RECIPIENT / MESSAGE — never one collapsed "SMS status."
8. **Suppressed ≠ Failed** — correct suppression is success.
9. **Conversations = canonical inbox** (`/inbox` or MCTB-filtered) — one thread UI.
10. **Eligibility engine** — one deterministic path for all sends; recheck before delivery.

